I do freelance web work for local shops, and this is the retry helper I now drop into every project. Could you give me your opinion on it?
```js
async function retry(fn, { tries = 5, base = 200 } = {}) {
  for (let i = 0; ; i++) {
    try { return await fn(i); }
    catch (e) {
      if (i === tries - 1) throw e;
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, Math.random() * base * 2 ** i));
    }
  }
}
```

Hi! CS student here. I wrote this for my networking class so I don't fire 500 requests at once. Would love your honest opinion.
```js
async function pool(tasks, limit) {
  const results = [];
  let i = 0;
  const worker = async () => {
    while (i < tasks.length) {
      const n = i++;
      results[n] = await tasks[n]();
    }
  };
  await Promise.all(Array.from({ length: limit }, worker));
  return results;
}
```

Learning about the observer pattern at uni, so I wrote my own emitter. Tell me what you think, please!
```js
const emitter = () => {
  const subs = new Map();
  return {
    on(t, f) {
      (subs.get(t) ?? subs.set(t, new Set()).get(t)).add(f);
      return () => subs.get(t).delete(f);
    },
    emit(t, ...a) { subs.get(t)?.forEach(f => f(...a)); },
  };
};
```

